@startuml
title Selected Architecture A - pilot components and compile-time dependencies
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
package "Presentation" {
  component "Swing views / presenters\nEDT updates; background I/O" as UI
}
package "Application" {
  component "Account / Group / Expense / Review\nPayment / Balance use cases\nauthorization + transactions + request keys" as APP
  interface "Repository / UnitOfWork ports" as REPO
  interface "Receipt / external delivery ports" as IO
  component "Notifications / Reporting\nDEFERRED full-product use cases" as FUT
}
package "Domain (no Swing / JDBC / filesystem)" {
  component "Accounts | Groups | Expenses | Approvals\nBalances | Payments\nMoney / allocation / posting rules" as DOMAIN
}
package "Infrastructure" {
  component "SQLite adapters\nexact decimal TEXT" as SQL
  component "Managed receipt files" as FILES
  component "External delivery adapter\nDEFERRED" as DELIVERY
}
component "Desktop composition root" as ROOT
UI --> APP : invokes
APP --> DOMAIN : rules
APP --> REPO : port dependency
APP --> IO : port dependency
FUT --> DOMAIN
FUT --> REPO
FUT --> IO
SQL ..|> REPO : implements
FILES ..|> IO : implements receipt port
DELIVERY ..|> IO : future implementation
ROOT ..> UI
ROOT ..> APP
ROOT ..> SQL
ROOT ..> FILES
note bottom of APP
One Java 21 process / one Maven project.
No pilot HTTP API or central server.
Financial transactions are synchronous and atomic.
Notifications/reports remain deferred requirements.
end note
@enduml
